#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""obsidian-track-changes-agent: read and write Track Changes marks (CriticMarkup) in a Markdown note, safely.

Why: agents hand-writing CriticMarkup get it wrong (wrong signature format, marks wrapped
across lines, a disk write into a note open in a suggesting-mode plugin that the plugin then
wraps as the human's own suggestion). Every agent uses this tool instead of typing marks.
Part of the obsidian-track-changes-agent Claude Code plugin (bin/obsidian-track-changes-agent, on the Bash PATH while the
plugin is enabled; `obsidian-track-changes-agent install-links` also links it into ~/.local/bin).

Format (default): the Obsidian Track Changes plugin's, a key="value" signature before the mark:
    {author="Claude (editor)" date="YYYY-MM-DD"~~old~>new~~}
    {author="…" date="…"++added++}  {author="…" date="…"--removed--}  {author="…" date="…">>comment<<}
--format inkling writes Inkling's {"author":…}@@ form instead (Inkling loops on the human's
own undo and accept in Suggesting mode; keep it switched off).
Each mark is written on one line. A mark signed "Claude (…)" is an agent's; any other author,
or none, is the human's.

Who may do what:
    comment              any agent (--as <role>)
    suggest              the editor only
    accept               the editor only, and only the HUMAN's suggestions (marks
                         not signed "Claude (…)")
    reject               NO agent, ever. The editor may only `comment`,
                         encouraging the human to reject their own suggestion.
    agents' suggestions  accepted or rejected by the human alone, in Obsidian
    block                the editor only: replace whole lines (a paragraph, a
                         bullet) with new lines, e.g. one bullet -> parent +
                         sub-bullets. Each old line becomes its own one-line
                         deletion, each new line its own one-line addition,
                         with indentation, the list marker and newlines
                         OUTSIDE the marks (so Track Changes and a renderer
                         show them as bullets). Old lines must hold no marks.
    tidy                 the editor only: removes the empty lines a resolved
                         block leaves inside a bullet list (whitespace only).
    watch                any agent: wait (cheaply) until the human adds or changes
                         a mark (comment, suggestion; any non-"Claude" author or
                         unsigned) in the watched notes, let their editing settle,
                         then exit with a summary. Exit 2 at once if a Sync
                         conflict copy appears. Remembers what it reported, so
                         a re-armed watcher neither repeats nor misses marks.
    revise               the editor only, and only its OWN pending suggestions:
                         replaces a stretch holding several of them with ONE
                         new suggestion whose old side is the original text
                         (those suggestions rejected). Nothing is accepted;
                         the human reviews the result. Refused if the stretch
                         holds the human's marks or anyone else's comments.
    resolve (a comment)  the editor only. An agent's comment: freely. The HUMAN's
                         comment: only with --addressed-by M, where M is a
                         pending editor suggestion the human will see; the
                         comment text moves next to M, quoted, so the human
                         reviews the change together with what they asked for.
"editor" means the one agent that owns the note's text in that project.
The tool enforces this; bypassing it by editing the raw marks is forbidden.

Safety:
- Refuse every write while the human's hold switch is on: a hold file at or above the
  note, up to the vault or repository root (`.track-changes-hold` or
  `track-changes-hold.md`; the watchbill plugin's `.watchbill-hold` and
  `watchbill-hold.md` count too, so a system using both has one switch).
- Writes are allowed while the note is open in Obsidian (Track Changes
  reloads them cleanly).
- Refuse while a Sync conflict copy of the note exists
  ("<note> (Conflicted copy <device> <time>).md"): two devices collided, and
  Sync's auto-merge may have blended stale and new text. The 5-second quiet
  wait sees only this machine's file, never another device's open, unsynced
  editor.
- Before writing: refuse if Inkling is enabled in the note's vault (it
  captures any disk write into an open note as the human's suggestion and
  loops). Then wait until the file has not changed for 5 seconds, so the
  write doesn't land mid-keystroke (gives up after 60 s).
- After writing: wait 3 seconds, re-read, and confirm the change is still
  there. If Obsidian saved over it, exit 3 and say so; nothing is retried
  blindly.
- Every write takes an exclusive lock, re-reads the file inside it, edits by
  matching text (not line numbers) and replaces the file atomically, so two
  agents writing at once can't lose each other's changes.

Commands:
    list     <file> [--author A] [--json]      pending marks, numbered in file order
    check    <file>                            exit 1 on unsigned, nested or malformed marks
    is-open  <file>                            exit 0 if open in Obsidian, 1 if not
    hold     <file>                            exit 4 and name the hold file if the hold is on, else 0
    suggest  <file> --as editor --old T [--new T] [--why T]
    suggest  <file> --as editor --insert T (--after A | --before A) [--why T]
    comment  <file> --as ROLE --text T (--on N | --after A)
    accept   <file> N --as editor               accept the human's suggestion N
    block    <file> --as editor --first T --last T --new-file F [--why T]
                                                replace whole lines with new lines
    tidy     <file> --as editor                 drop empty lines left inside lists
    watch    <file|dir>... [--pattern P] [--interval 10] [--settle 20] [--timeout 1800] [--json]
                                                exit 0 + summary on the human's new marks;
                                                2 on a conflict copy; 1 on timeout (re-arm)
    revise   <file> --as editor --marks 3,4,5 (--new T | --new-file F) [--why T]
                                                fold own pending suggestions into one;
                                                over several lines: one multi-line mark
    resolve  <file> N --as editor [--addressed-by M]
                                                remove comment N (the human's: needs M)
    install-links [--check] [--dry-run] [--bin-dir D] [--dev DIR] [--from NAME@MARKETPLACE] [--force]
                                                link this command into ~/.local/bin

Exit codes: 0 done; 1 check found problems, watch timed out, or is-open says not open;
2 watch saw a conflict copy, or a usage error; 3 a write did not stick; 4 the hold is on (`hold`);
any refusal exits non-zero with "obsidian-track-changes-agent: refused: <why>" on stderr.

Environment (all optional): TRACK_CHANGES_QUIET (5), TRACK_CHANGES_MAX_WAIT (60) and
TRACK_CHANGES_VERIFY_DELAY (3) in seconds; TRACK_CHANGES_STATE, the block-record file
(~/.local/state/track-changes/blocks.json; watch state sits beside it); TRACK_CHANGES_OBSIDIAN,
Obsidian's command line tool ("obsidian"; empty: never call it). The CRITICMARKUP_* names of the
earlier criticmarkup.py are read when the new ones are unset.

Library use: parse(text) -> [mark dict] and is_agent(author) are stable for callers that load
this file as a module.
"""
import argparse, fcntl, hashlib, json, os, re, sys, tempfile, time
from pathlib import Path

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True

VERSION = "0.1.5"
PROG = "obsidian-track-changes-agent"


def env(name, default):
    """TRACK_CHANGES_<name>, else the earlier CRITICMARKUP_<name>, else default."""
    for prefix in ("TRACK_CHANGES_", "CRITICMARKUP_"):
        v = os.environ.get(prefix + name)
        if v is not None:
            return v
    return default


# --- the human's hold switch ---------------------------------------------------------------

HOLD_NAMES = (".track-changes-hold", "track-changes-hold.md", ".watchbill-hold", "watchbill-hold.md")


def hold_for(path):
    """The hold file governing `path`, or ''. The search starts at the note's folder and walks
    up to the first folder holding `.obsidian` or `.git` (the vault or repository root), or to
    the home folder. A visible `.md` name exists because Obsidian cannot create a dotfile and
    its Sync does not carry hidden files, so a hold set from a phone needs a visible name.
    The human creates and deletes the file; agents never do."""
    p = os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(str(path) or "."))
    d = p if os.path.isdir(p) else os.path.dirname(p)
    home = os.path.expanduser("~")
    while True:
        for name in HOLD_NAMES:
            f = os.path.join(d, name)
            if os.path.isfile(f):
                return f
        parent = os.path.dirname(d)
        if (os.path.isdir(os.path.join(d, ".obsidian")) or os.path.exists(os.path.join(d, ".git"))
                or d == home or parent == d):
            return ""
        d = parent


def describe_hold(hold):
    try:
        since = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M", time.localtime(os.path.getmtime(hold)))
    except OSError:
        since = "unknown"
    return f"{hold} (set {since})"


KINDS = {"++": ("addition", "++"), "--": ("deletion", "--"), "~~": ("substitution", "~~"),
         ">>": ("comment", "<<"), "==": ("highlight", "==")}
OPEN = re.compile(r"\{(\+\+|--|~~|>>|==)")
SIG = re.compile(r'^\{[^{}]*\}@@', re.S)              # Inkling: {"author":…}@@
TC_SIG = re.compile(r'^(?:\w+="[^"]*"\s*)+')          # Track Changes: author="…" date="…"


class Refused(SystemExit):
    def __init__(self, msg):
        super().__init__(f"{PROG}: refused: {msg}")


def parse(text):
    """Every mark as a dict, in file order. Track Changes' prefix form
    ({author="…"++…++}) is recognised too, for listing and checking."""
    marks, i = [], 0
    pat = re.compile(r'\{(?:\w+="[^"]*"\s*)*(\+\+|--|~~|>>|==)')
    while True:
        m = pat.search(text, i)
        if not m:
            return marks
        kind, close = KINDS[m.group(1)]
        end = text.find(close + "}", m.end())
        if end < 0:
            marks.append({"start": m.start(), "end": len(text), "kind": kind, "error": "unclosed"})
            return marks
        end += len(close) + 1
        raw = text[m.start():end]
        body = text[m.end():end - len(close) - 1]
        prefix = text[m.start() + 1:m.end() - 2]
        mk = {"start": m.start(), "end": end, "kind": kind, "raw": raw, "author": None, "time": None}
        sig = SIG.match(body)
        if sig:
            try:
                meta = json.loads(sig.group(0)[:-2])
                mk["author"], mk["time"] = meta.get("author"), meta.get("time")
            except json.JSONDecodeError:
                mk["error"] = "bad signature JSON"
            body = body[sig.end():]
        elif prefix.strip():
            a = re.search(r'author="([^"]*)"', prefix)
            d = re.search(r'date="([^"]*)"', prefix)
            mk["author"], mk["format"] = (a.group(1) if a else None), "obsidian-track-changes-agent"
            if d:
                mk["date"] = d.group(1)     # shown by `list`; not part of a mark's identity for `watch`
        if kind == "substitution":
            old, sep, new = body.partition("~>")
            mk["old"], mk["new"] = old, new
            if not sep:
                mk["error"] = "substitution without ~>"
        else:
            mk["text"] = body
        if OPEN.search(body) or pat.search(body):
            mk["error"] = "nested mark inside"
        if "\n" in raw:
            mk["multiline"] = True
        marks.append(mk)
        i = end


def is_agent(author):
    return bool(author) and author.startswith("Claude")


def vault_of(path):
    for d in [path.parent, *path.parent.parents]:
        if (d / ".obsidian").is_dir():
            return d
    return None


def obsidian_cli():
    """Obsidian's command line tool, or None when switched off (TRACK_CHANGES_OBSIDIAN="")."""
    return env("OBSIDIAN", "obsidian") or None


def cli_tabs():
    """Names of open markdown tabs from Obsidian's own CLI (live, via IPC), or
    None when the CLI can't answer. It may only see one window's tabs, so it is
    combined with workspace.json, never trusted alone (tested)."""
    import subprocess
    cli = obsidian_cli()
    if not cli:
        return None
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([cli, "tabs"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return None
    return {line.split("] ", 1)[1].strip() for line in r.stdout.splitlines()
            if line.startswith("[markdown] ")}


def is_open(path):
    """True if the note may be open in Obsidian. Conservative: open if either
    the live CLI tab list has a markdown tab with this note's name, or the
    saved workspace.json (main and pop-out windows; read only) lists it, or
    either source can't be read. Over-blocking is safe; under-blocking lets
    Inkling capture an agent's write as the human's suggestion."""
    vault = vault_of(path)
    if not vault:
        return False
    tabs = cli_tabs()
    if tabs and path.stem in tabs:
        return True
    ws = vault / ".obsidian" / "workspace.json"
    try:
        data = json.loads(ws.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):
        return True        # can't tell: assume open, refuse to write
    rel = str(path.resolve().relative_to(vault.resolve()))
    found = []

    def walk(n):
        if isinstance(n, dict):
            st = n.get("state")
            if n.get("type") == "leaf" and isinstance(st, dict) and st.get("state", {}).get("file") == rel:
                found.append(n)
            for v in n.values():
                walk(v)
        elif isinstance(n, list):
            for v in n:
                walk(v)
    walk(data)
    return bool(found)


FORMAT = "trackchanges"      # set from --format


def mark(op, role, body):
    """One signed mark. op: '++', '--', '~~' (body 'old~>new'), '>>'.
    inkling:       {++{"author":"Claude (editor)","time":<unix s>}@@body++}
    trackchanges:  {author="Claude (editor)" date="YYYY-MM-DD"++body++}"""
    close = {"++": "++", "--": "--", "~~": "~~", ">>": "<<"}[op]
    if FORMAT == "trackchanges":
        return f'{{author="Claude ({role})" date="{time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")}"{op}{body}{close}}}'
    sig = json.dumps({"author": f"Claude ({role})", "time": int(time.time())},
                     ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":"))   # compact, as Inkling writes it
    return f"{{{op}{sig}@@{body}{close}}}"


def flex(phrase):
    """Regex for a phrase that may wrap across lines in the file."""
    words = phrase.split()
    if not words:
        raise Refused("empty text")
    return re.compile(r"\s+".join(re.escape(w) for w in words))


class Span:
    """A matched phrase: .start(), .end(), .group(0), like a re.Match."""
    def __init__(self, text, start, end):
        self.text, self.s, self.e = text, start, end
    def start(self): return self.s
    def end(self): return self.e
    def group(self, _=0): return self.text[self.s:self.e]


def find_unique(text, phrase, marks):
    """The one occurrence of phrase outside existing marks. Line wraps in the
    file are matched by any whitespace; a leading or trailing space given in
    the phrase is kept ("very " deletes the word and its space)."""
    hits = [m for m in flex(phrase).finditer(text)
            if not any(mk["start"] < m.end() and m.start() < mk["end"] for mk in marks)]
    if len(hits) != 1:
        raise Refused(f"{phrase!r} occurs {len(hits)} times outside existing marks; give a longer, unique phrase")
    s, e = hits[0].start(), hits[0].end()
    if phrase[:1].isspace() and s > 0 and text[s - 1] == " ":
        s -= 1
    if phrase[-1:].isspace() and e < len(text) and text[e] == " ":
        e += 1
    return Span(text, s, e)


def one_line(s):
    return re.sub(r"\s*\n\s*", " ", s)


QUIET_SECONDS = float(env("QUIET", 5))         # the human idle this long first
QUIET_MAX_WAIT = float(env("MAX_WAIT", 60))    # then give up
VERIFY_DELAY = float(env("VERIFY_DELAY", 3))   # let Obsidian react


def glob_escape(name):
    return re.sub(r"([*?\[\]])", r"[\1]", name)


def inkling_enabled(path):
    """True if Inkling is enabled in the note's vault (community-plugins.json,
    read only; plus Obsidian's CLI when it answers)."""
    vault = vault_of(path)
    if not vault:
        return False
    try:
        listed = json.loads((vault / ".obsidian" / "community-plugins.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):
        listed = []
    if "inkling" in listed:
        return True
    import subprocess
    cli = obsidian_cli()
    if not cli:
        return False
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([cli, "plugins:enabled", "filter=community", f"vault={vault.name}"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
        return r.returncode == 0 and "inkling" in r.stdout.split()
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return False


def wait_quiet(path):
    """Wait until the file hasn't changed for QUIET_SECONDS (the human not typing)."""
    deadline = time.time() + QUIET_MAX_WAIT
    while True:
        idle = time.time() - path.stat().st_mtime
        if idle >= QUIET_SECONDS:
            return
        if time.time() + (QUIET_SECONDS - idle) > deadline:
            raise Refused(f"{path.name} keeps changing (edited {idle:.0f} s ago); the human is probably typing. "
                          "Try again later")
        time.sleep(QUIET_SECONDS - idle + 0.2)


def change_marker(old, new):
    """What the edit looks like in context: left context + new middle + right
    context, from trimming the common prefix and suffix of old and new."""
    p = 0
    while p < min(len(old), len(new)) and old[p] == new[p]:
        p += 1
    q = 0
    while q < min(len(old), len(new)) - p and old[-1 - q] == new[-1 - q]:
        q += 1
    left, right = old[max(0, p - 40):p], old[len(old) - q:len(old) - q + 40]
    return left + new[p:len(new) - q] + right


def write(path, change):
    """Inkling check, wait for quiet, lock, re-read, apply change(text) -> new
    text, replace atomically, then confirm the change stuck. Refused while the
    human's hold switch is on."""
    hold = hold_for(path)
    if hold:
        raise Refused(f"the human's hold switch is on: {describe_hold(hold)}. No writer may change {path.name} "
                      "while it exists. Wait until the human deletes it; do not remove it yourself")
    conflicts = sorted(path.parent.glob(f"{glob_escape(path.stem)} (Conflicted copy*{path.suffix}"))
    if conflicts:
        raise Refused(f"Obsidian Sync conflict copies of {path.name} exist ({', '.join(c.name for c in conflicts)}). "
                      "Another device edited it at the same time. Ask the human to reconcile them first")
    if inkling_enabled(path):
        raise Refused("Inkling is enabled in this vault. It captures any write into an open note as the human's "
                      "suggestion, and loops. Ask the human to disable it first")
    wait_quiet(path)
    # The lock keeps the earlier tool's name on purpose: while copies of criticmarkup.py are still
    # in use, both tools must take the same lock on the same note.
    lock = Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / f"criticmarkup-{hashlib.sha1(str(path.resolve()).encode()).hexdigest()[:16]}.lock"
    with open(lock, "w") as lf:
        fcntl.flock(lf, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        text = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        new = change(text)
        fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=f".{PROG}-", dir=path.parent)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            f.write(new)
        os.chmod(tmp, path.stat().st_mode & 0o777)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    marker = change_marker(text, new)
    time.sleep(VERIFY_DELAY)
    now = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    if marker not in now:
        print(f"{PROG}: WARNING: the change did not stick: {path.name} changed again within "
              f"{VERIFY_DELAY:.0f} s and no longer contains it (Obsidian or another writer saved over it). "
              "Run `list` to see the current state before trying again.", file=sys.stderr)
        raise SystemExit(3)
    return new


def numbered(text):
    return list(enumerate(parse(text), 1))


def pick(text, n):
    for i, mk in numbered(text):
        if i == n:
            if mk.get("error"):
                raise Refused(f"mark {n} is malformed ({mk['error']}); fix it by hand with the human's OK")
            return mk
    raise Refused(f"no mark {n}; run `list` again (numbers shift as marks are resolved)")


def need_editor(role, what):
    if role != "editor":
        raise Refused(f"only the editor may {what} (you are {role!r})")


def cmd_list(a):
    text = a.file.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    rows = []
    for i, mk in numbered(text):
        if a.author and a.author.lower() not in (mk.get("author") or "").lower():
            continue
        line = text.count("\n", 0, mk["start"]) + 1
        when = (time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M", time.localtime(mk["time"])) if mk.get("time")
                else mk.get("date") or "")
        what = (f"{one_line(mk.get('old',''))!r} -> {one_line(mk.get('new',''))!r}" if mk["kind"] == "substitution"
                else repr(one_line(mk.get("text", ""))))
        rows.append({"n": i, "line": line, "kind": mk["kind"], "author": mk.get("author") or "(unsigned)",
                     "time": when, "what": what, "problem": mk.get("error") or "", "multiline": bool(mk.get("multiline"))})
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(rows, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))
    for r in rows if not a.json else []:
        flag = f"  !! {r['problem']}" if r["problem"] else ("  (spans lines)" if r["multiline"] else "")
        print(f"#{r['n']:<3} L{r['line']:<4} {r['kind']:<12} {r['author']:<22} {r['time']:<16} {r['what'][:90]}{flag}")
    if not rows and not a.json:
        print("no pending marks")


def cmd_check(a):
    text = a.file.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    bad, notes = [], []
    for i, mk in numbered(text):
        line = text.count("\n", 0, mk["start"]) + 1
        if mk.get("error"):
            bad.append(f"#{i} L{line}: {mk['error']}")
        if mk.get("multiline"):
            notes.append(f"#{i} L{line}: note: spans lines (written by `revise`, or by the human in Track Changes)")
        if not mk.get("author"):
            bad.append(f"#{i} L{line}: unsigned")
        elif FORMAT == "inkling" and mk.get("format") == "obsidian-track-changes-agent":
            bad.append(f"#{i} L{line}: Track Changes signature; Inkling can't show it")
        elif FORMAT == "trackchanges" and mk.get("format") != "obsidian-track-changes-agent":
            bad.append(f"#{i} L{line}: Inkling signature; Track Changes shows it as text")
    if notes:
        print("\n".join(notes))
    print("\n".join(bad) if bad else f"OK: every mark is signed, {FORMAT} format, not nested")
    return 1 if bad else 0


def cmd_is_open(a):
    o = is_open(a.file)
    print("open in Obsidian" if o else "not open")
    return 0 if o else 1


def cmd_suggest(a):
    need_editor(a.role, "suggest text changes")
    why = mark(">>", a.role, one_line(a.why)) if a.why else ""

    def change(text):
        marks = parse(text)
        if a.insert is not None:
            anchor = a.after or a.before
            if not anchor:
                raise Refused("--insert needs --after or --before")
            m = find_unique(text, anchor, marks)
            new_mark = mark("++", a.role, one_line(a.insert)) + why
            at = m.end() if a.after else m.start()
            return text[:at] + new_mark + text[at:]
        if a.old is None:
            raise Refused("give --old (with --new to replace, without to delete) or --insert")
        m = find_unique(text, a.old, marks)
        old = one_line(m.group(0))
        new_mark = (mark("~~", a.role, f"{old}~>{one_line(a.new)}") if a.new is not None
                    else mark("--", a.role, old)) + why
        return text[:m.start()] + new_mark + text[m.end():]
    write(a.file, change)
    print("suggestion written")


def cmd_comment(a):
    def change(text):
        new_mark = mark(">>", a.role, one_line(a.text))
        if a.on is not None:
            at = pick(text, a.on)["end"]
        elif a.after:
            at = find_unique(text, a.after, parse(text)).end()
        else:
            raise Refused("give --on N (comment on mark N) or --after TEXT")
        return text[:at] + new_mark + text[at:]
    write(a.file, change)
    print("comment written")


def resolve_mark(mk, accept):
    """The text a mark leaves behind when accepted (accept=True is the only
    path agents use; False is kept for completeness and tests)."""
    k = mk["kind"]
    if k == "addition":
        return mk["text"] if accept else ""
    if k == "deletion":
        return "" if accept else mk["text"]
    if k == "substitution":
        return mk["new"] if accept else mk["old"]
    if k == "highlight":
        return mk["text"]
    return ""


def cmd_accept(a):
    need_editor(a.role, "accept the human's suggestions")

    def change(text):
        mk = pick(text, a.n)
        if mk["kind"] == "comment":
            raise Refused(f"mark {a.n} is a comment; use `resolve`")
        if is_agent(mk.get("author")):
            raise Refused(f"mark {a.n} is {mk['author']}'s suggestion; only the human accepts or rejects agents' "
                          "suggestions, in Obsidian")
        attached = [c for c in parse(text) if c["kind"] == "comment" and c["start"] == mk["end"]]
        if attached:
            raise Refused(f"suggestion {a.n} has an open comment ({attached[0].get('author') or 'unsigned'}: "
                          f"{one_line(attached[0].get('text',''))[:60]!r}); it must be answered and resolved first")
        return text[:mk["start"]] + resolve_mark(mk, True) + text[mk["end"]:]
    write(a.file, change)
    print("accepted")


STATE = Path(env("STATE", Path.home() / ".local/state/track-changes/blocks.json"))
LEGACY_STATE_DIR = Path.home() / ".local/state/criticmarkup"     # the earlier criticmarkup.py's


def read_state(name):
    """A state file's JSON from the state folder; when it is missing there and no state path was
    set, the earlier tool's copy, so block records and watch baselines carry over. None if neither."""
    paths = [STATE.parent / name]
    if not os.environ.get("TRACK_CHANGES_STATE") and not os.environ.get("CRITICMARKUP_STATE"):
        paths.append(LEGACY_STATE_DIR / name)
    for p in paths:
        try:
            return json.loads(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except FileNotFoundError:
            continue
        except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):
            return None
    return None


def load_blocks():
    blocks = read_state(STATE.name)
    return blocks if isinstance(blocks, list) else []


def save_blocks(blocks):
    STATE.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    STATE.write_text(json.dumps(blocks, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1), encoding="utf-8")


def cmd_block(a):
    """Replace whole lines with new lines as one-line tracked marks, and record
    where the block sits (anchors = nearest non-empty lines around it) and what
    the region must read once accepted or rejected, so `tidy` can restore it
    exactly. The record lives outside the vault (STATE)."""
    need_editor(a.role, "suggest text changes")
    new_lines = Path(a.new_file).read_text(encoding="utf-8").rstrip("\n").split("\n")
    if not any(l.strip() for l in new_lines):
        raise Refused("--new-file is empty; to delete text use `suggest --old`")
    sig_why = mark(">>", a.role, one_line(a.why)) if a.why else ""
    record = {}

    def change(text):
        lines = text.split("\n")
        def only(needle, what):
            hits = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if needle in l]
            if len(hits) != 1:
                raise Refused(f"--{what} {needle!r} matches {len(hits)} lines; give text unique to one line")
            return hits[0]
        i, j = only(a.first, "first"), only(a.last, "last")
        if j < i:
            raise Refused("--last comes before --first")
        old = lines[i:j + 1]
        if any(parse(l) for l in old) or any(OPEN.search(l) for l in old):
            raise Refused("the old lines hold marks; resolve or revise them first")
        if not any(l.strip() for l in old):
            raise Refused("the old lines are empty")

        def wrap(line, op):
            """Indentation AND the list marker stay outside the mark, so the
            Typst template, Track Changes and Obsidian still see a bullet."""
            if not line.strip():
                return line
            m = re.match(r"^(\s*(?:[-*+]|\d+\.)\s+|\s*)(.*)$", line)
            return m.group(1) + mark(op, a.role, m.group(2))
        out = [wrap(l, "--") for l in old] + [wrap(l, "++") for l in new_lines]
        out[-1] += sig_why
        above = max([k for k in range(i) if lines[k].strip()], default=-1)
        below = min([k for k in range(j + 1, len(lines)) if lines[k].strip()], default=len(lines))
        record.update({
            "file": str(a.file.resolve()), "id": f"b{time.time_ns()}",
            "above": lines[above] if above >= 0 else None,
            "below": lines[below] if below < len(lines) else None,
            "rejected": lines[above + 1:below],
            "accepted": lines[above + 1:i] + new_lines + lines[j + 1:below],
        })
        return "\n".join(lines[:i] + out + lines[j + 1:])
    write(a.file, change)
    blocks = load_blocks(); blocks.append(record); save_blocks(blocks)
    print("block suggestion written: old lines as tracked deletions, new lines as tracked additions. "
          "After the human resolves them in Track Changes, run `tidy`.")


EMPTYISH = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:(?:[-*+]|\d+\.)\s*)?$")   # blank, or a bare list marker left by a resolved line


def is_emptyish(line):
    return bool(EMPTYISH.match(line))


def lstrip_empty(lines):
    k = 0
    while k < len(lines) and not lines[k].strip():
        k += 1
    return lines[k:]


def rstrip_empty(lines):
    k = len(lines)
    while k > 0 and not lines[k - 1].strip():
        k -= 1
    return lines[:k]


def nonempty(lines):
    return [l.rstrip() for l in lines if not is_emptyish(l)]


def cmd_tidy(a):
    """For each recorded block of this file whose marks are all resolved, make
    the region read exactly as accepted or as rejected (removing the empty
    lines Track Changes leaves). Touches nothing outside recorded blocks."""
    need_editor(a.role, "tidy")
    me = str(a.file.resolve())
    blocks = load_blocks()
    mine = [b for b in blocks if b["file"] == me]
    if not mine:
        raise Refused("no recorded block suggestions for this note")
    report, done = [], set()

    def change(text):
        report.clear(); done.clear()
        lines = text.split("\n")
        for b in mine:
            def find(anchor, lo):
                if anchor is None:
                    return None
                hits = [k for k in range(lo, len(lines)) if lines[k] == anchor]
                return hits[0] if len(hits) == 1 else "ambiguous"
            ia = -1 if b["above"] is None else find(b["above"], 0)
            if ia == "ambiguous" or (b["above"] is not None and ia is None):
                report.append(f"{b['id']}: can't find the line above the block; left alone"); continue
            ib = len(lines) if b["below"] is None else find(b["below"], ia + 1)
            if ib == "ambiguous" or ib is None:
                report.append(f"{b['id']}: can't find the line below the block; left alone"); continue
            region = lines[ia + 1:ib]
            if parse("\n".join(region)):          # any mark, either signature style
                report.append(f"{b['id']}: still has pending marks; left alone"); continue
            if nonempty(region) == nonempty(b["accepted"]):
                lines[ia + 1:ib] = b["accepted"]; report.append(f"{b['id']}: accepted, restored exactly")
            elif nonempty(region) == nonempty(b["rejected"]):
                lines[ia + 1:ib] = b["rejected"]; report.append(f"{b['id']}: rejected, restored exactly")
            else:   # mixed decisions: keep the region's own leading/trailing gaps, drop inner empties
                r = b["rejected"]
                lead = len(r) - len(lstrip_empty(r))
                trail = len(r) - len(rstrip_empty(r))
                kept = [l for l in region if not is_emptyish(l)]
                lines[ia + 1:ib] = r[:lead] + kept + (r[len(r) - trail:] if trail else [])
                report.append(f"{b['id']}: mixed accept/reject; empty lines inside the block removed")
            done.add(b["id"])
        return "\n".join(lines)
    new = change(a.file.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    if new != a.file.read_text(encoding="utf-8"):
        write(a.file, change)
    save_blocks([b for b in blocks if b["id"] not in done])
    print("\n".join(report) if report else "nothing to tidy")


def watch_targets(paths, pattern):
    files = []
    for p in paths:
        p = Path(p)
        if p.is_dir():
            files += sorted(f for f in p.glob(pattern) if " " not in f.name)
        elif p.is_file():
            files.append(p)
    return [f.resolve() for f in files]


def mark_key(mk):
    """Identity of a mark for 'already reported': kind, author, time, content."""
    body = mk.get("text") if "text" in mk else f"{mk.get('old')}~>{mk.get('new')}"
    return f"{mk['kind']}|{mk.get('author') or ''}|{mk.get('time') or ''}|{body}"


def human_marks(path):
    text = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    out = []
    for i, mk in numbered(text):
        if not is_agent(mk.get("author")):
            line = text.count("\n", 0, mk["start"]) + 1
            what = (f"{one_line(mk.get('old',''))!r} -> {one_line(mk.get('new',''))!r}" if mk["kind"] == "substitution"
                    else repr(one_line(mk.get("text", ""))))
            out.append({"key": mark_key(mk), "file": str(path), "n": i, "line": line, "kind": mk["kind"],
                        "author": mk.get("author") or "(unsigned)", "what": what[:200]})
    return out


def cmd_watch(a):
    files = watch_targets(a.paths, a.pattern)
    if not files:
        raise SystemExit(f"{PROG} watch: nothing to watch")
    state_path = STATE.parent / f"watch-{hashlib.sha1('|'.join(map(str, files)).encode()).hexdigest()[:12]}.json"
    prior = read_state(state_path.name)
    seen, first_run = (set(prior), False) if isinstance(prior, list) else (set(), True)
    if first_run and not a.report_existing:      # baseline: what is there now counts as seen
        seen = {m["key"] for f in files for m in human_marks(f)}
        state_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        state_path.write_text(json.dumps(sorted(seen)), encoding="utf-8")

    def conflicts():
        return [c for f in files for c in f.parent.glob(f"{glob_escape(f.stem)} (Conflicted copy*{f.suffix}")]

    def fresh():
        return [m for f in files if f.exists() for m in human_marks(f) if m["key"] not in seen]

    def report(code, items, headline):
        if a.json:
            print(json.dumps({"status": headline, "items": items}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))
        else:
            print(headline)
            for m in items:
                print(f"  {Path(m['file']).name}:{m['line']}  #{m['n']} {m['kind']} by {m['author']}: {m['what']}")
        return code

    deadline = time.time() + a.timeout if a.timeout else None
    mtimes = {f: f.stat().st_mtime for f in files if f.exists()}
    pending = fresh()                              # marks that arrived while no watcher ran
    while True:
        c = conflicts()
        if c:
            return report(2, [{"file": str(x), "n": 0, "line": 0, "kind": "conflict copy", "author": "Obsidian Sync",
                               "what": x.name} for x in c],
                          "CONFLICT: an Obsidian Sync conflict copy appeared; agents must not write until the human reconciles it")
        changed = [f for f in files if f.exists() and f.stat().st_mtime != mtimes.get(f)]
        if changed:
            for f in changed:
                mtimes[f] = f.stat().st_mtime
            pending = fresh()
        if pending:
            # let the human finish: wait until every watched file has been idle for --settle seconds
            while True:
                newest = max(f.stat().st_mtime for f in files if f.exists())
                idle = time.time() - newest
                if idle >= a.settle:
                    break
                time.sleep(min(a.settle - idle + 0.5, a.settle))
            pending = fresh()
            if pending:
                seen.update(m["key"] for m in pending)
                state_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
                state_path.write_text(json.dumps(sorted(seen)), encoding="utf-8")
                return report(0, pending, f"NEW: {len(pending)} new or changed mark(s) by the human")
        if deadline and time.time() >= deadline:
            return report(1, [], "TIMEOUT: no new marks by the human; re-arm the watch")
        time.sleep(a.interval)


def parse_marks_arg(spec):
    """'3,4,7-12' -> sorted unique numbers."""
    out = set()
    for part in spec.split(","):
        part = part.strip()
        if not part:
            continue
        m = re.fullmatch(r"(\d+)\s*-\s*(\d+)", part)
        if m:
            lo, hi = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))
            if hi < lo:
                raise Refused(f"bad range {part!r}")
            out.update(range(lo, hi + 1))
        elif part.isdigit():
            out.add(int(part))
        else:
            raise Refused(f"bad --marks entry {part!r}; use 3,4,7-12")
    return sorted(out)


LIST_PREFIX = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:(?:[-*+]|\d+[.)])\s+)?$")      # indentation and an optional list marker only
SENTINEL = "\x00"


def revise_original(text, start, end, inside):
    """The stretch text[start:end] with every one of the editor's own marks
    rejected and its comments dropped. A line whose only content was a rejected
    addition (the bare "- " a block's added bullet leaves) is dropped whole."""
    out, pos = [], start
    for mk in sorted(inside, key=lambda m: m["start"]):
        out.append(text[pos:mk["start"]])
        if mk["kind"] == "comment":
            out.append(SENTINEL)
        else:
            r = resolve_mark(mk, False)
            out.append(r if r else SENTINEL)
        pos = mk["end"]
    out.append(text[pos:end])
    kept = []
    for line in "".join(out).split("\n"):
        if SENTINEL in line:
            line = line.replace(SENTINEL, "")
            if is_emptyish(line):
                continue
        kept.append(line)
    return "\n".join(kept)


def cmd_revise(a):
    """Replace the editor's own pending suggestions in a stretch by ONE new suggestion.
    The stretch may span lines: the result is then one mark spanning those lines (one
    Track Changes card, accepted or rejected whole), which Track Changes 2.2.0 parses
    and applies as a unit (main.js: node offsets, oldText/newText)."""
    need_editor(a.role, "revise its own suggestions")
    me = f"Claude ({a.role})"
    wanted = parse_marks_arg(a.marks)
    if not wanted:
        raise Refused("give --marks N[,N…] (ranges like 3-12 are fine)")
    if (a.new is None) == (a.new_file is None):
        raise Refused("give exactly one of --new TEXT or --new-file FILE")
    new_text = a.new if a.new is not None else Path(a.new_file).read_text(encoding="utf-8").rstrip("\n")
    dropped = []

    def change(text):
        dropped.clear()
        marks = numbered(text)
        chosen = [mk for i, mk in marks if i in wanted]
        if len(chosen) != len(wanted):
            raise Refused("some mark numbers don't exist; run `list` again")
        start, end = min(m["start"] for m in chosen), max(m["end"] for m in chosen)
        # the editor's own reason comments right after the last chosen mark go too
        grew = True
        while grew:
            grew = False
            for i, mk in marks:
                if mk["start"] == end and mk["kind"] == "comment" and mk.get("author") == me:
                    end, grew = mk["end"], True
        inside = [mk for _, mk in marks if mk["start"] >= start and mk["end"] <= end]
        for mk in inside:
            if mk.get("error"):
                raise Refused(f"a mark in the stretch is malformed ({mk['error']})")
            if mk.get("author") != me:
                raise Refused(f"the stretch holds a {mk['kind']} by {mk.get('author') or 'unsigned'}; "
                              "only your own pending suggestions can be revised. Marks by the human or other "
                              "roles stay: ask the human to reject the card, or have the comment answered first")
        # whole-stretch overlap guard: a mark that straddles the stretch edge is not "inside"
        for _, mk in marks:
            if (mk["start"] < end and start < mk["end"]) and mk not in inside:
                raise Refused("a mark straddles the edge of the stretch; revise whole marks only")
        original = revise_original(text, start, end, inside)
        line_start = text.rfind("\n", 0, start) + 1
        original_full = text[line_start:start] + original            # as whole lines, for the block-record match
        new = new_text
        multi = "\n" in text[start:end] or "\n" in original or "\n" in new
        if multi:
            # the first line's indentation and list marker stay outside the mark, when old and new share them
            head = text[line_start:start]
            if LIST_PREFIX.match(head) and head != "":
                if new.startswith(head):
                    new = new[len(head):]
                else:
                    start, original = line_start, head + original
        else:
            original, new = one_line(original), one_line(new)
        if original.strip() == new.strip():
            raise Refused("the revision equals the original text; nothing to suggest")
        op = "++" if not original.strip() else "--" if not new.strip() else "~~"
        closers = {"++": ["++}"], "--": ["--}"], "~~": ["~>", "~~}"]}[op]
        for label, body in (("old", original), ("new", new)):
            if OPEN.search(body) or parse(body) or any(c in body for c in closers + ["<<}"]):
                raise Refused(f"the {label} text contains CriticMarkup syntax ({', '.join(closers)}, <<}} or a mark); "
                              "remove it or write it differently")
        new_mark = (mark("++", a.role, new) if op == "++"
                    else mark("--", a.role, original) if op == "--"
                    else mark("~~", a.role, f"{original}~>{new}"))
        if a.why:
            new_mark += mark(">>", a.role, one_line(a.why))
        dropped.append(set(l.strip() for l in original_full.split("\n") if l.strip()))
        return text[:start] + new_mark + text[end:]
    write(a.file, change)
    # block records (for `tidy`) of lines now folded into this one mark are obsolete: nothing is left to tidy
    if dropped:
        orig = dropped[0]
        blocks = load_blocks()
        keep = [b for b in blocks
                if b.get("file") != str(a.file.resolve())
                or not (set(l.strip() for l in b.get("rejected", []) if l.strip()) <= orig and b.get("rejected"))]
        if len(keep) != len(blocks):
            save_blocks(keep)
    print("revised: one suggestion replaces", len(wanted), "of yours")


def cmd_resolve(a):
    need_editor(a.role, "resolve comments")

    def change(text):
        mk = pick(text, a.n)
        if mk["kind"] != "comment":
            raise Refused(f"mark {a.n} is a {mk['kind']}, not a comment")
        if is_agent(mk.get("author")):
            return text[:mk["start"]] + text[mk["end"]:]
        # The human's comment: only once a pending editor suggestion addresses it.
        if a.addressed_by is None:
            raise Refused(f"comment {a.n} is the human's. Make a suggestion that addresses it, then "
                          f"`resolve {a.n} --addressed-by <that suggestion's number>`")
        sug = pick(text, a.addressed_by)
        if sug["kind"] in ("comment", "highlight") or sug.get("author") != f"Claude ({a.role})":
            raise Refused(f"mark {a.addressed_by} is not a pending suggestion of yours "
                          f"({sug['kind']} by {sug.get('author') or 'unsigned'}); the human must see a change")
        quoted = one_line(mk["text"]).replace("<<}", "<< }")
        note = mark(">>", a.role, f"Addresses the human's comment: \"{quoted}\"")
        # remove the human's comment, then put the quoted note right after the suggestion
        # (and after any comments already attached to it)
        cut = text[:mk["start"]] + text[mk["end"]:]
        sug_end = sug["end"] - (len(mk["raw"]) if mk["start"] < sug["start"] else 0)
        at = sug_end
        for later in parse(cut):
            if later["start"] == at and later["kind"] == "comment":
                at = later["end"]
        return cut[:at] + note + cut[at:]
    write(a.file, change)
    print("comment resolved")


def cmd_hold(a):
    hold = hold_for(a.file)
    if hold:
        print(f"on: {describe_hold(hold)}")
        return 4
    print("off")
    return 0


# --- install-links: put the command on PATH outside Claude Code ------------------------------

PLUGIN_NAME = "obsidian-track-changes-agent"


def plugins_file():
    """Claude Code's record of installed plugins: under $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR when set, else ~/.claude.
    TRACK_CHANGES_PLUGINS_FILE overrides it (the tests use this)."""
    if os.environ.get("TRACK_CHANGES_PLUGINS_FILE"):
        return Path(os.environ["TRACK_CHANGES_PLUGINS_FILE"])
    config = Path(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or Path.home() / ".claude").expanduser()
    return config / "plugins" / "installed_plugins.json"


def installed_bin(plugins_file, pick=None):
    """(bin dir, 'name@marketplace version') of the user-scope install of this plugin."""
    try:
        data = json.loads(Path(plugins_file).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise SystemExit(f"{PROG} install-links: cannot read {plugins_file}: {e}")
    found = []
    for key, entries in (data.get("plugins") or {}).items():
        if key.split("@", 1)[0] != PLUGIN_NAME or (pick and key != pick):
            continue
        for e in entries if isinstance(entries, list) else [entries]:
            if e.get("scope") == "user" and e.get("installPath"):
                found.append((key, e))
    if not found:
        raise SystemExit(f"{PROG} install-links: no user-scope {PLUGIN_NAME} install{' ' + pick if pick else ''} in "
                         f"{plugins_file}: install the plugin first (claude plugin install {PLUGIN_NAME}@<marketplace>)")
    if len(found) > 1:
        raise SystemExit(f"{PROG} install-links: more than one user-scope {PLUGIN_NAME} install: "
                         + ", ".join(k for k, _ in found) + "; pick one with --from NAME@MARKETPLACE")
    key, e = found[0]
    root = Path(e["installPath"])
    for b in (root / "bin", root / "plugin" / "bin"):
        if (b / PROG).is_file():
            return b, f"{key} {e.get('version', '?')}"
    raise SystemExit(f"{PROG} install-links: {key}: no bin/{PROG} under its installPath {root} "
                     "(stale entry? run `claude plugin update`)")


def dev_bin(path):
    root = Path(path).expanduser().resolve()
    for b in (root / "plugin" / "bin", root / "bin"):
        if (b / PROG).is_file():
            return b, f"working tree {root}"
    raise SystemExit(f"{PROG} install-links: --dev {path}: no plugin/bin/{PROG} or bin/{PROG} under it")


ALIASES = ()      # other names to link; the track-changes alias was dropped in 0.1.3


def cmd_install_links(a):
    """Link ~/.local/bin/obsidian-track-changes-agent to the installed plugin's copy, or a working
    tree's with --dev. Atomic: the command is never missing
    from PATH mid-switch. Re-run after each plugin update."""
    src_bin, what = dev_bin(a.dev) if a.dev else installed_bin(plugins_file(), a.pick)
    bin_dir = Path(a.bin_dir).expanduser().resolve()
    print(f"source: {src_bin} ({what})")
    bad = 0
    for name in (PROG, *ALIASES):
        target, link = src_bin / name, bin_dir / name
        old = os.readlink(link) if link.is_symlink() else ""
        if not os.access(target, os.X_OK):
            print(f"missing {target}: not an executable file; left {link} alone")
            bad += 1
            continue
        if link.is_symlink() and os.path.realpath(link) == os.path.realpath(target):
            print(f"ok      {link} -> {target}")
            continue
        state = "repoint" if link.is_symlink() else "blocked" if os.path.lexists(link) else "create"
        if a.check or (state == "blocked" and not a.force):
            why = {"repoint": f"points at {old}", "create": "does not exist",
                   "blocked": "is a file, not a symlink" + ("" if a.check else " (--force replaces it)")}[state]
            print(f"{'differs' if a.check else 'refused'} {link} {why}")
            bad += 1
            continue
        if a.dry_run:
            print(f"would   {link} -> {target}" + (f" (was {old})" if old else ""))
            continue
        bin_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        tmp = bin_dir / f".{name}.link-tmp"
        if os.path.lexists(tmp):
            tmp.unlink()
        os.symlink(target, tmp)
        os.replace(tmp, link)
        print(f"linked  {link} -> {target}" + (f" (was {old})" if old else ""))
    if a.dry_run:
        print("dry run: nothing changed.")
    if not a.check and str(bin_dir) not in os.environ.get("PATH", "").split(os.pathsep):
        print(f"note: {bin_dir} is not on your PATH")
    return 1 if bad else 0


def main(argv=None):
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=PROG, description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    p.add_argument("--version", action="version", version=f"{PROG} {VERSION}")
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    def add(name, role=False):
        s = sub.add_parser(name)
        s.add_argument("file", type=Path)
        if role:
            s.add_argument("--as", dest="role", required=True, help="your role: editor, checker, …")
        return s
    s = add("list"); s.add_argument("--author"); s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    add("check"); add("is-open"); add("hold")
    s = add("suggest", True)
    s.add_argument("--old"); s.add_argument("--new"); s.add_argument("--insert")
    s.add_argument("--after"); s.add_argument("--before"); s.add_argument("--why")
    s = add("comment", True); s.add_argument("--text", required=True)
    s.add_argument("--on", type=int); s.add_argument("--after")
    s = sub.add_parser("watch", help="wait for the human's new marks; exit with a summary")
    s.add_argument("paths", nargs="+", help="notes, or folders (with --pattern)")
    s.add_argument("--pattern", default="*.md", help="glob inside a folder (e.g. 'variant-*.md')")
    s.add_argument("--interval", type=float, default=10, help="seconds between cheap mtime checks")
    s.add_argument("--settle", type=float, default=20, help="seconds of no edits before reporting")
    s.add_argument("--timeout", type=float, default=1800, help="give up after this many seconds (0 = never)")
    s.add_argument("--report-existing", action="store_true", help="first run: report marks already present")
    s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    s = add("block", True); s.add_argument("--first", required=True); s.add_argument("--last", required=True)
    s.add_argument("--new-file", required=True, help="file holding the new lines, indentation included"); s.add_argument("--why")
    add("tidy", True)
    s = add("revise", True); s.add_argument("--marks", required=True, help="your pending suggestions, e.g. 3,4,5 or 7-12")
    s.add_argument("--new"); s.add_argument("--new-file", help="file with the new text, several lines allowed"); s.add_argument("--why")
    for name in ("accept", "resolve"):
        s = add(name, True); s.add_argument("n", type=int)
    s.add_argument("--addressed-by", type=int, help="resolve: the editor suggestion that addresses the human's comment")
    # No `reject`: no agent may reject a suggestion. To argue against one of the human's,
    # `comment --on N` and let them reject it.
    s = sub.add_parser("install-links", help="link this command into ~/.local/bin, for use outside Claude Code")
    s.add_argument("--check", action="store_true", help="report only; exit 1 unless the link is right")
    s.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    s.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="replace a regular file in the way")
    s.add_argument("--bin-dir", default="~/.local/bin")
    s.add_argument("--dev", help="link a working tree's copy instead of the installed plugin's")
    s.add_argument("--from", dest="pick", help="NAME@MARKETPLACE when more than one install exists")
    p.add_argument("--format", choices=("trackchanges", "inkling"), default="trackchanges",
                   help="signature format for new marks: trackchanges (default; the human reviews with the "
                        "Track Changes plugin) or inkling (Inkling's {json}@@ form; keep Inkling off)")
    a = p.parse_args(argv)
    global FORMAT
    FORMAT = a.format
    if a.cmd == "watch":
        return cmd_watch(a)
    if a.cmd == "install-links":
        return cmd_install_links(a)
    if not a.file.is_file():
        raise SystemExit(f"{PROG}: {a.file}: no such file")
    return {"list": cmd_list, "check": cmd_check, "is-open": cmd_is_open, "hold": cmd_hold, "suggest": cmd_suggest,
            "comment": cmd_comment, "accept": cmd_accept, "block": cmd_block, "tidy": cmd_tidy, "revise": cmd_revise,
            "resolve": cmd_resolve}[a.cmd](a)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
